            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0124" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/570: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador to the Greek Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-23T18:00:00+03:00">May 23, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 24—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek 168. My Greek 166, May 22, 6 p.m. Mr. Papandreou has been entrusted with
                    the formation of the Government of National Unity. It is reported that the
                    number of portfolios which seems certain to be large and their apportionment
                    among the various parties and organizations was clearly settled at the last
                    meeting of the conference. As the delegates are now all in Cairo it is believed
                    that Papandreou will complete his task very shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
